  "answer": "For pricing questions, use the authoritative-source strategy: treat NL-003 as the single source of truth, since it states it is the sole basis for sales proposals, renewals, and audits and forbids deprecated or informal pricing models [NL-003#NL-003-S01]. For metrics questions, use the official metrics/performance documents — NL-012, NL-016, and NL-001 — and avoid relying on anecdotal sales-call statements, because those official reports contain the actual churn, NPS, onboarding, and revenue data [NL-012#NL-012-S09], [NL-016#NL-016-S03], [NL-001#NL-001-S04].\n\nFor cross-document business recommendations, use a reconciliation strategy that prioritizes official current metrics over narrative sales material and prior sales-call strategy. For example, NL-016 and NL-012 both direct focus toward regulated mid-market and enterprise customers and away from SMBs [NL-016#NL-016-S03], [NL-012#NL-012-S09], which overrides the small-team enthusiasm found in the sales call transcript [NL-023#NL-023-S03].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
